# =============================================================================
# Frontend build context exclusions
# =============================================================================
# node_modules and .output are the important ones: both are host-built, both
# are large, and both are regenerated inside the image. Copying them in would
# be slower AND could smuggle a Windows-built binary or a stale Cloudflare
# Worker bundle into a Linux Node image.
# =============================================================================

# --- Secrets and local env ----------------------------------------------------
# VITE_* values are compiled into the browser bundle, so they are supplied as
# build args instead - never by copying a developer's .env into the context.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
**/.dev.vars

# --- Host-built dependencies and output ---------------------------------------
# `**/` matters: Docker matches a bare `node_modules/` only at the context
# root, so nested copies would otherwise be shipped into the build context.
**/node_modules/
**/.output/
**/.nitro/
**/.vinxi/
**/.tanstack/
**/dist/
**/dist-ssr/
**/.wrangler/

# --- Alternative package manager ----------------------------------------------
# This project standardised on npm + package-lock.json; the Dockerfile runs
# `npm ci`. A stray bun.lock invites CI and the image to disagree.
bun.lock
bunfig.toml
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml

# --- Superseded code ----------------------------------------------------------
_to_delete/
_ts_backup.tar.gz

# --- Supabase CLI project (migrations run against hosted Supabase) ------------
supabase/

# --- Version control, tooling and editor noise --------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
.lovable/
eslint.config.js
.prettierrc
.prettierignore

# --- Docs, logs, scratch ------------------------------------------------------
**/*.md
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
